// Test: two array literals written against each other are reported as that.
//
// A type name hard against a ']' makes the brackets a size, and a '[' there is an element
// type -- `[2][]i64` is two empty `[]i64`. So `[1 2][3 4]` reads the second '[' as the first
// one's element type and finds a size inside it. Reporting that as a size in an array type
// sends the reader looking for a type they did not write; the two literals want a space.
fn main() {
	[[1 2][3 4]] -> g
	g len print nl
}
